    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Yes, it is already possible. In 'mini.visits' it is a common design that empty string for either `path` or `cwd` means \"all available\". Same is true for [`remove_label()`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/964fab7fecd14f66a69a96162f8aa816480690fd/doc/mini-visits.txt#L532-L537). But that works for one label at a time. So in your case it would be these three calls:\r\n```lua\r\nMiniVisits.remove_label('core', '', '')\r\nMiniVisits.remove_label('tmp', '', '')\r\nMiniVisits.remove_label('test', '', '')\r\n```",
            "created_at": "2023-12-01T08:38:10Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/599#issuecomment-1835689384",
